      "recallAtK": 1,
      "reciprocalRank": 1,
      "answer": "Playwright performs several checks on an element before it clicks it to ensure the action behaves as expected. These checks include:\n\n- Ensuring the locator resolves to exactly one element.\n- Checking if the element is visible.\n- Verifying the element is stable, meaning it is not animating or in the process of completing an animation.\n- Confirming the element receives pointer events, which means it is the hit target of the pointer event at the action point.\n- Ensuring the element is enabled.\n- Checking if the element is not inert.\n\nThese checks help to prevent actions from occurring on elements that might not be interactable or might not respond as expected.",
      "citedDocs": [],
      "inputTokens": 1090,
