      "recallAtK": 1,
      "reciprocalRank": 1,
      "answer": "To stub an API response in a Playwright test, you can use the `page.route` method to intercept the request and provide a custom response. Here's a simple example:\n\n```js\nawait page.route('**/api/fetch_data', route => route.fulfill({\n  status: 200,\n  body: testData,\n}));\n```\n\nRegarding third-party services, the advice is to avoid testing them directly. Instead, you should mock the responses from third-party services using Playwright's network API. This ensures that your tests are faster, more reliable, and less dependent on external factors.",
