      "recallAtK": 1,
      "reciprocalRank": 1,
      "answer": "The assertion is failing due to a timeout, even though the test timeout is set much longer, because the assertion itself has a separate timeout by default. The default assertion timeout is 5 seconds, which is shorter than the test timeout.\n\nTo retry a custom value until it matches, you can use async matchers that automatically retry, such as `expect(page.getByTestId('status')).toHaveText('Submitted')`. These matchers will keep checking the condition until it is met or until their timeout is reached.\n\nIf you need to customize the retry behavior, you can adjust the `property: TestConfig.expect` value in your test config. For example, you can set a custom timeout for assertions:\n\n```js\nimport { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  expect: {\n    timeout: 10000, // 10 seconds\n  },\n});\n```\n\nThis will set the assertion timeout to 10 seconds for all tests in your project. If you need more granular control, you can use the `page.waitForSelector` method with a custom timeout:\n\n```js\nawait page.waitForSelector('button', { timeout: 10000 });\n```\n\nThis will wait up to 10 seconds for the selector to appear.",
